    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phintĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				city in Sicily</i>, now <i>Alicata</i> or <i>Licata</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 83, § 192</span></i>.
			—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phintĭenses</span></b> , ĭum,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of Phintia</i>,
				<i>the Phintians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8,
				14, § 91</span></i>.</div>
